sn4.6:4.1 starts: “He who resorts to empty huts for
sn4.6:4.2 starts: He is the sage, self-controlled.
sn45.34:6.2 starts: Having left behind sensual pleasures.
sn45.34:6.3 starts: Owning nothing, the wise man
sn45.34:6.4 starts: Should cleanse himself of mental defilements.
sn45.4:10.1 starts: “Good will, harmlessness, and seclusion:
sn45.4:10.2 starts: These are the chariot’s weaponry,
sn47.18:6.1 starts: “The seer of the destruction of birth,
sn47.18:6.2 starts: Compassionate, knows the one-way path
